tools/calibrate_cost.py:2:"""Fit the per-class cost weights against paired measurements.
tools/calibrate_cost.py-3-
tools/calibrate_cost.py-4-Input: a JSON file with candidates = [{name, hist: {mnemonic: count},
tools/calibrate_cost.py-5-<machine>: ticks_per_call}]. For each machine column a linear model
tools/calibrate_cost.py-6-  ticks ~= sum_c w_c * count_c
tools/calibrate_cost.py-7-is fitted (non-negative least squares via projected gradient), and the fit is
tools/calibrate_cost.py-8-compared with a count-only model. This is the v0 calibration for the
tools/calibrate_cost.py-9-docs/09 resource lower-bound cost model, not a vendor uarch model.
tools/calibrate_cost.py-10-
