     1	"""Critical-path latency estimator over AArch64 disassembly (v0).
     2	
     3	The linear throughput cost model failed to rank the M14-M16 candidates
     4	(R2 < 0): latency on these kernels is dominated by the dependency chain. This
     5	module builds a register + stack-slot def-use graph from objdump text and
     6	computes the longest forward latency path (no parallelism modeling), which is
     7	an upper bound usable for *ranking* candidates within one kernel family.
     8	
     9	Stack accesses are tracked as pseudo-registers `sp#offset`, so a
    10	store-to-coef / load-from-coef round trip (proto_c) correctly contributes to
    11	the chain.
    12	"""
